==German==

===Etymology===
From {{der|de|gml|helfte}}, derived from {{m|gml|half||half}}. The form entered early modern German via [[Central German]]. The alternation ''-b-'' ↔ ''-ft-'' between {{m|de|halb}} and ''Hälfte'' has not been levelled, probably because the same alternation occurs also—for different reasons—in native [[High German]] words (compare {{m|de|schreiben}} ↔ {{m|de|Schrift}}). Cognate with {{cog|nl|helft}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhɛlftə/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Hälfte.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Hälften}}

# [[half]]; fifty [[percent]] of something
#: {{ux|de|Jeder von uns kriegt die '''Hälfte'''.|Each of us gets '''half'''.}}
# [[half]], [[share]]; any of two [[correlate|correlating]] [[piece]]s, whatever the size
#: {{ux|de|Ich will die größere '''Hälfte'''!|I want the bigger '''half'''!}}
# {{lb|de|chiefly|informal}} [[middle]]; the virtual line where two equal halves meet
#: {{ux|de|Hier ist die '''Hälfte''' vom Spielfeld.|This is the '''middle''' of the pitch.}}

